{"name":"Fountain Frolic","hex":"#e4e4c5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fountain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A natural source of water; a spring.","An artificial, usually ornamental, water feature (usually in a garden or public place) consisting of one or more streams of water originating from a statue or other structure."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To flow or gush as if from a fountain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fountain"},{"term":"frolic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Merry, joyous, full of mirth; later especially, frolicsome, sportive, full of playful mischief. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Free; liberal; bountiful; generous."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make merry; to have fun; to  romp; to behave playfully and uninhibitedly.","To cause to be merry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frolic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fountain","blocks":[{"text":"A fountain, from the Latin \"fons\", meaning source or spring, is a decorative reservoir used for discharging water. It is also a structure that jets water into the air for a decorative or dramatic effect in landscapes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Fountains_Collage.jpg/330px-Fountains_Collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountain"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Dendera_Tempel_19.JPG/500px-Dendera_Tempel_19.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Dendera_Tempel_19.JPG/1280px-Dendera_Tempel_19.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Dendera_Tempel_19.JPG/500px-Dendera_Tempel_19.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse